 "notes": "CardDemo's Db2 transaction-type list (transaction CTLI, program COTRTLIC, admin menu option 5): seven types a page from CARDDEMO.TRANSACTION_TYPE through two Db2 cursors (C-TR-TYPE-FORWARD, and C-TR-TYPE-BACKWARD for PF7), optionally filtered by type code and by a description LIKE pattern; 'D' or 'U' on a row and ENTER asks for confirmation, PF10 DELETEs or UPDATEs it; PF2 goes to COTRTUPC, PF3 back to the admin menu. The paging state, the rows shown and the pending action live in the program's COMMAREA area after CARDDEMO-COMMAREA (rows never fetched are LOW-VALUES); each scenario gives the state the previous screen returned. Both sides run their SQL on one real Db2 (tests/tools/equivalence_db2.py): TRANSACTION_TYPE and TRANSACTION_TYPE_CATEGORY are created from the corpus DDL, seeded before each scenario and both compared after it. The seed is the corpus's DB2LTTYP.ctl and DB2LTCAT.ctl INSERTs unchanged, plus five types (08-12) without category rows in a separate INSERT, written for this case (and carddemo-cotrtupc): the corpus's seven types fill exactly one page, so paging needs more, and a type without category rows can be deleted. Not covered: every path through 9999-FORMAT-DB2-MESSAGE, which CALLs Db2's DSNTIAC (not modelled) -- a delete refused by the category foreign key (-532), an update or delete of a row gone meanwhile (+100), cursor and priming-query errors; and the PF3-from-COTRTUPC / re-entered-from-another-program resets, which no CardDemo caller produces (COTRTUPC clears its CARDDEMO-COMMAREA on entry, so its PF3 always returns to the admin menu). Derived from CardDemo (Apache-2.0; Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): LICENSE and NOTICE here are the source's own."
